{"id":34174711672112,"type":"artist","name":"Nena","artist":null,"year":null,"weight":55,"info":{"img":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/Nena_Dein_Song_2008.jpg?width=500","bio":"Nena nació el 24 de marzo de 1960 en Hagen, (Renania del Norte-Westfalia). Es una cantante alemana que alcanzó la fama gracias a la canción \"99 Luftballons\" (\"99 Red Balloons\" en la versión en ingles). Con el relanzamiento de sus propios éxitos, la carrera de Nena experimentó un segundo aire en el año 2002.\n\nNena nació como Gabriele Susanne Kerner el 24 de marzo de 1960 en Hagen, Renania del Norte-Westfalia, Alemania.Desde los tres años de edad le apodaron Nena.","tags":["pop","german","new wave","80s","female vocalists"]},"works":[{"id":162446171133541,"type":"album","name":"Nena","artist":"Nena","year":1983,"weight":3,"yt":"TgHX_IzSNLY","src":"musthear","from":{"books":[],"podcasts":[],"lists":[{"id":155080497509792,"name":"RYM Top — Scenes & Movements — Neue Deutsche Welle","rank":21,"scaruffi":null}],"n_lists":1}},{"id":189539166361956,"type":"song","name":"99 Luftballons","artist":"Nena","year":1984,"weight":8,"yt":"Fpu5a0Bl8eY","src":"books,singles","from":{"books":[{"name":"Loops 1 y 2","title":"Loops 1 y 2. Una historia de la música electrónica (Javier Blánquez (ed.))"}],"podcasts":[],"lists":[{"id":26942126325510,"name":"Billboard Year-End 1984","rank":28,"scaruffi":null}],"n_lists":1}},{"id":180155576179955,"type":"song","name":"99 Luftballons/99 Red Balloons","artist":"Nena","year":1984,"weight":2,"yt":null,"src":"charts","from":{"books":[],"podcasts":[],"lists":[{"id":132335824845498,"name":"Billboard Year-End Hot 100","rank":28,"scaruffi":null}],"n_lists":1}},{"id":244395363826926,"type":"song","name":"99 Red Balloons","artist":"Nena","year":1984,"weight":9,"yt":"hiwgOWo7mDc","src":"ensayos,singles","from":{"books":[],"podcasts":[{"name":"The Ongoing History of New Music","n":2}],"lists":[{"id":179984359651109,"name":"UK nº1 · 1980s","rank":532,"scaruff